Checkstyle: A static code analysis tool specifically for Java. It checks source code against a set of coding standards (e.g., naming conventions, whitespace, and formatting) to ensure team-wide consistency.
SonarScanner: The "engine" that runs on your local machine or CI server. It scans your source code, executes analysis (including Checkstyle rules if configured), and uploads the results to the SonarQube server.
SonarQube: A central platform that hosts the dashboards for code quality and security. It receives data from the SonarScanner to track bugs, vulnerabilities, and "code smells" over time.
Nexus (Sonatype): An artifact repository manager. Once the code passes analysis and is built into a "package" (like a JAR file), Nexus stores and versions these artifacts so they can be safely used in deployment.




